#!/usr/bin/env sh
#
# Probe whether the OpenAI Batch API accepts the `store` parameter on a
# Responses request, and whether OpenAI honors it.
#
# The synchronous path is covered by unit specs, which assert the body Raif
# builds. The Batch API takes that same body inside a JSONL line and validates
# it asynchronously, so a parameter OpenAI rejects there surfaces as a per-entry
# error in the batch's error file rather than as a response to any call Raif
# makes. Only a live batch shows that.
#
# The probe reports three things, in increasing strength:
#   1. `store` is present in the input file OpenAI actually holds.
#   2. Every entry came back completed rather than errored.
#   3. GET /v1/responses/<id> 404s, which is what store: false means.
#
# It submits a real batch and costs real money. Two entries on the default
# nano model is a fraction of a cent. A batch usually ends within a few
# minutes, but OpenAI's completion window is 24h, so the probe can time out
# with the batch still running - it prints a --resume command for that case.
#
# Usage:
#   bin/probe_open_ai_batch_store [options]
#
# Options:
#   -m, --model KEY         Raif model key to batch (default: open_ai_responses_gpt_5_4_nano)
#       --store             Send store: true instead, as a control run
#   -n, --entries N         Entries in the batch (default: 2)
#       --poll SECONDS      Seconds between status polls (default: 20)
#       --timeout SECONDS   Give up waiting after this long (default: 900)
#       --resume BATCH_ID   Poll an existing Raif::ModelCompletionBatch instead of submitting
#       --cancel-on-timeout Ask OpenAI to cancel the batch if the timeout is reached
#
# Environment variables:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY          Required
#
# Exit codes:
#   0  every entry completed
#   1  an entry failed, or credentials/model selection was wrong
#   2  timed out with the batch still running
#
# Examples:
#   bin/probe_open_ai_batch_store
#   bin/probe_open_ai_batch_store --store
#   bin/probe_open_ai_batch_store --model open_ai_responses_gpt_5_6_terra
#   bin/probe_open_ai_batch_store --resume 7

set -eu

bundle exec spec/dummy/bin/rails runner script/probe_open_ai_batch_store.rb "$@"
